   "turn": 4,
   "reply": "{\"action\": \"finish\"}\n\nI fixed `top_words` in `words.py`. It now lowercases the text and extracts words with the regex `[A-Za-z']+`, so \"don't\" is one word and \"well-known\" splits into two. It counts them, sorts by count descending and then alphabetically, and returns the first k as `(word, count)` tuples.\n\nI ran it on `\"Don't stop. don't STOP well-known well known, it's it's\"` and got `[(\"don't\", 2), (\"it's\", 2), ('known', 2), ('stop', 2), ('well', 2)]`, which is the expected result. I did not test edge cases such as k = 0 or text with no words.",
